Title: "Fecal trnL Metabarcoding Reliably Reconstructs Plant Intake and Reveals Multi-Omics Links to Gut Microbiota and Host Metabolism"

Authors: 
N. Andrea Villota-Salazar¹*, 
Oscar Javier Lara-Guzmán¹, 
Juan S. Escobar-Restrepo¹*  

¹Vidarium – Nutrition, Health and Wellness Research Center  
2023–2026

output:
  html_document:
    toc: true
    number_sections: true
    code_folding: hide

This script contains the analytical workflow used to integrate fecal trnL metabarcoding data, gut microbiota profiles, and untargeted plasma metabolomics data.

Samples were obtained from a nutritional intervention study involving daily consumption of golden berry (Physalis peruviana) for three weeks (DOI: 10.1016/j.foodres.2022.111949). Biological samples were collected at baseline (no golden berry consumption) and after three weeks of daily intake.

